      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "MISS DEFY (6) is the one to beat off a sharp BM66 second at Albury, where she travelled kindly and closed within just under two lengths of Fair Master. She is proven at the 2000m with two wins and two placings from six attempts, has won at this track and distance, and the quick back-up is a positive. SNAP DECISION (2) brings the best recent Nowra line, finishing third as favourite after being slow away and suffering interference near the home turn, with Brodie Loy back aboard after a win from two rides on him. MIDNIGHT AFFAIR (1) has been around the mark in BM66 and BM65 grade, beaten just under a length by Marsabit at Wagga after placing at this venue the run prior, and the 2kg claim helps offset the big impost. PURE MELODY (4) is the progressive danger after charging home to win a Class 1 at this track, with barrier one and a sound jockey-horse record keeping her in the mix.",
